  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A conducting wire of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100\"></span> g and length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> cm is moving horizontally in a magnetic field. The kinetic energy of the wire is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\"></span> J and the induced emf in the wire is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.0 \\times 10^{-4}\"></span> V. </p>\n<p>What is the magnitude of the vertical component of the magnetic field at the wire’s position?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\"></span> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\mu\"></span>T</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"400\"></span> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\mu\"></span>T</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">40 mT</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">400 mT</li>\n</ol>"
